# Credentials — never commit. See docs/STANDARDS.md section 10.
.env
.env.*
*.key
*_key
*_token
secrets.*
credentials.*
config.local.*

# Snapshots ARE committed. They are the preservation archive, and the whole
# point is that they survive — a few megabytes a month is a cheap price, and the
# monthly workflow commits them automatically. If the repository ever gets
# unwieldy (say past a couple of gigabytes), move older years to a Zenodo
# deposit and prune them here, with a changelog note saying where they went.
# The provenance log is always committed.
data/processed/
*.zip
*.parquet

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# OS and editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
